intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINJO, SOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORII AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINJO SOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORII, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINJO, SOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A digital broadcasting receiver in which one decoder decodes both Reed-Solomon codes for TMCC and Reed-Solomon codes of an MPEG2-TS packet of a main signal. The received data is divided into a main signal and a TMCC signal. When the separated main signal is subjected to deinterleaving by a deinterleaving circuit (503), the burst symbol signal is eliminated, and the TMCC signal separated subsequent to the main signal in the last frame of a superframe is added by a selector (509). The received data to which the TMCC signal is added is decoded by a basic Reed-Solomon code decoder (510) so as to carry out the error correction of the main signal and the TMCC signal.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un récepteur de radiodiffusion numérique dans lequel un décodeur est destiné à décoder des codes Reed-Solomon pour TMCC et des codes Reed-Solomon d'un paquet MPEG2-TS d'un signal principal. Les données reçues sont divisées en un signal principal et en un signal TMCC. Une fois ledit signal principal soumis à un désentrelacement effectué au moyen d'un circuit de désentrelacement (503), le signal de symbole en rafale est éliminé, et ledit signal TMCC séparé du signal principal dans la dernière trame d'une supertrame est ajouté à l'aide d'un sélecteur (509). Les données reçues auxquelles le signal TMCC est ajouté sont alors décodées par un décodeur de code Reed-Solomon standard (510), de manière à effectuer la correction d'erreurs du signal principal et du signal TMCC.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>